WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:19.300
Part nine: your own return. Anil Kumar Demo - made up, like everyone in these films - is salaried and holds a few mutual funds. He signed up as an individual, was approved at once, and his one client is himself. He opens My return.

2
00:00:19.906 --> 00:00:28.356
Five steps: gather, check, choose, review and file. Each ticks itself off as it is done.

3
00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:36.718
First, a checklist of what to keep handy. Each line ticks itself as the document comes in.

4
00:00:37.328 --> 00:00:43.378
And where each document comes from: who issues it, and what it gives the return.

5
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:51.149
He starts with the pre-filled JSON from the e-filing portal. Drop it in, and read it.

6
00:00:51.765 --> 00:00:56.445
Then Form 16 from his employer, as a PDF.

7
00:00:57.047 --> 00:01:09.027
The A I S PDF is locked the department's way: his P A N in small letters and his date of birth. He types it once - the eye shows what he typed.

8
00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:18.690
The 26 A S; his C A M S capital-gains statement, as a C S V; and his bank statement.

9
00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:40.684
Every document shows what was read from it: salary and tax deducted from Form 16, interest and dividends from the A I S, four sales from C A M S, and the interest in his bank statement.

10
00:01:41.281 --> 00:01:53.881
Later he downloads the 26 A S again and drops it in - and is asked first: replace the one he has, or keep both. Nothing is overwritten without asking.

11
00:01:54.484 --> 00:02:03.464
History keeps it all: each document added, the 26 A S replaced - and the old one kept, ready to download.

12
00:02:04.061 --> 00:02:12.631
At the top, his return at a glance: total income, tax, and the refund due - kept up to date with every document.

13
00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:24.580
Check: Form 16's tax deducted beside the 26 A S, salary and interest beside the A I S. Here, everything agrees.

14
00:02:25.186 --> 00:02:30.586
Choose: both regimes worked out in full, and the cheaper one marked.

15
00:02:31.203 --> 00:02:34.943
And from income to tax, step by step.

16
00:02:35.561 --> 00:02:45.091
Next, part ten: the review - capital gains, a plot sold, a flat he co-owns, gifts - and the return, ready to file.
